What OAuth2 Uses Instead of Passwords

OAuth2 uses tokens:

Token	Purpose
Access Token	Used to call APIs
Refresh Token	Used to get a new access token
Real Banking Example 🏦

A finance management app wants to read your bank transactions.

Instead of giving your bank password, you:

1️⃣ Login to the bank website
2️⃣ Approve access for the finance app
3️⃣ Bank issues an OAuth2 access token
4️⃣ App uses the token to fetch transactions

Your password stays safe.

Advantages of OAuth2

✅ Passwords are never shared
✅ Secure delegated access
✅ Works with APIs and microservices
✅ Standard used by Google, Facebook, GitHub, etc.

