4️⃣ OAuth2 Flow with Refresh Tokens
Step-by-Step

Authorization Request – Client requests authorization from the user

Authorization Grant – User approves access → server issues authorization code

Access + Refresh Tokens – Client exchanges code for tokens

Access Protected API – Client includes access token in Authorization: Bearer <token> header

Refresh Token Flow – When access token expires:

POST /token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token=<REFRESH_TOKEN>&client_id=xyz

Server validates refresh token → issues new access token
This flow shows how a client obtains Access Tokens and Refresh Tokens, uses them to call APIs, and refreshes them when the access token expires.

1️⃣ Step-by-Step OAuth2 Flow
Step 1 — User Login & Authorization

The user logs in through the Authorization Server.

User → Client App → Authorization Server

User approves permission for the client to access resources.

Step 2 — Authorization Code Issued

The authorization server sends an authorization code to the client.

Authorization Server → Client
Authorization Code

This code is temporary and short-lived.

Step 3 — Exchange Code for Tokens

The client sends the authorization code to the authorization server to obtain tokens.

POST /oauth/token
grant_type=authorization_code
code=AUTH_CODE
client_id=client123
client_secret=secret

Server response:

{
  "access_token": "ACCESS_TOKEN",
  "refresh_token": "REFRESH_TOKEN",
  "expires_in": 3600
}
2️⃣ Access API Using Access Token

Client calls the resource server using the access token.

GET /api/account/balance
Authorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN

Resource server validates the token and returns the response.

3️⃣ Access Token Expires

Access tokens are short-lived.

Example:

Access Token Lifetime = 15 minutes

When it expires, the API will return:

401 Unauthorized
4️⃣ Use Refresh Token to Get New Access Token

Instead of asking the user to log in again, the client sends the refresh token.

POST /oauth/token
grant_type=refresh_token
refresh_token=REFRESH_TOKEN
client_id=client123

Server response:

{
  "access_token": "NEW_ACCESS_TOKEN",
  "expires_in": 3600
}
5️⃣ Continue API Requests

Client now uses the new access token.

Client → API with new Access Token

User session continues without logging in again.

