In OAuth2, the client first obtains an authorization code after the user logs in. The client exchanges this code for an access token and refresh token. The access token is used to access APIs and is short-lived. When it expires, the client sends the refresh token to the authorization server to obtain a new access token without requiring the user to log in again.

